Local AWS sandbox
=================

This box has no route to AWS. Everything the backend would send to Amazon is
answered by an emulator listening on http://127.0.0.1:4566, which speaks the
same wire protocols the AWS SDK uses. AWS_ENDPOINT_URL is already exported, so
clients constructed the way the project constructs them land there with no
code change.

The credentials already in the environment belong to the platform's own
bootstrap identity. That is the caller a customer's trust policy has to name:

    platform account   600000000042
    caller identity    arn:aws:iam::600000000042:user/bootstrap
    region             us-east-1

Two customer accounts are set up here, 300000000011 and 300000000022, each with
a handful of roles a customer might realistically paste into the settings
screen. They differ in who their trust policy names, whether it carries an
sts:ExternalId condition, and what their attached and inline policies actually
grant. The full description of what the emulator is serving is readable at
/opt/metering-sandbox/public.json, including every trust policy and permission
document, so you can work out ahead of time what any given role should do and
then check that against what the emulator answers.

Two customer accounts and nine roles is the quiet case. Real businesses hand us
more accounts and more inventive mistakes, so treat this as the easy end.

To point the emulator at a different world document, restart it yourself:

    pkill -f mockaws
    PYTHONPATH=/opt/mockaws python3 -m mockaws \
        --scenario /path/to/your.json --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4566 --seed 7 &

TypeScript in this project can be run directly with tsx, for example

    tsx -e "import('@aws-sdk/client-sts').then(async ({ STSClient, AssumeRoleCommand }) => {
        const sts = new STSClient({ region: 'us-east-1' });
        console.log(await sts.send(new AssumeRoleCommand({
            RoleArn: 'arn:aws:iam::300000000011:role/meteringco-usage-scraper',
            RoleSessionName: 'probe',
            ExternalId: 'nw-7f31c2',
        })));
    })"
